{"generated":"2026-10-11T04:18:52.166Z","flood_attached":false,"method":"Buildings: every way or multipolygon relation tagged building=* in the Geofabrik Puerto Rico extract of OpenStreetMap; one record per OSM object, outer ring only. ADDED footprints (buildings_added; buildings = buildings_osm + buildings_added): machine detections from imagery carried by Overture Maps release 2026-09-23.1 (Google Open Buildings, Microsoft ML Buildings), not surveyed, not in OpenStreetMap. OpenStreetMap is the base: every building of our own OSM extract is kept unchanged. An Overture building is added only if none of its sources is OpenStreetMap and (1) it does not overlap our OSM extract or an addition already accepted: dropped if its centroid is inside an OSM footprint, an OSM centroid is inside it, or the outlines intersect at all (outer rings); (2) it is plausible: at least 15 m2, confidence at least 0.7 where the source gives one, and not above 5000 m2 unless its confidence is at least 0.8; (3) its centroid is on land inside a municipio. Tests run in that order and a candidate is counted under the first one it fails. Added records have bit 7 (0x80) of kind set; kind is house under 400 m2, otherwise other; height is the source's own or 0. They count in every number here exactly like OSM buildings; their kind is a guess from area alone. Ground elevation: bilinear sample of the AWS Terrain Tiles Terrarium zoom-14 tile (USGS 3DEP 1/3 arc-second, about 10 m, on land) at the centroid of the outer ring; samples are clamped at the tile edge. It is the ground at one point, not the floor height. Flood class: NOT ATTACHED YET in this build (zone_counts are all class 0). at_or_below: inclusive counts of buildings with ground elevation <= 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2, 3 and 5 m (buildings below 0 included). Use these for \"at or below +X m\": the histogram bins are half-open, so summing bins 0..3 gives \"< 1.0 m\" and leaves out the buildings sitting on the exact 1.0 m terrace. buildings_sfha = classes